From: Ruhan van der Berg <35257374+RuhanSA079@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:16:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] soc: rapuyama: videocore: start_delay parameter

videocore.start_delay=N waits N seconds before the bring-up. On the N8 a
bring-up with loader B left the phone powered off with no USB shell and
no RAM log; with a delay the shell is up first and the bring-up can be
watched with dmesg -w.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/rapuyama/videocore.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/rapuyama/videocore.c b/drivers/soc/rapuyama/videocore.c
index 3f9c2c739..4608eb23d 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/rapuyama/videocore.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rapuyama/videocore.c
@@ -213,6 +213,12 @@ static bool partial;
 module_param(partial, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(partial, "push only the changed rows, BROKEN on the phone (the VC ignores the write rects)");
 
+/* wait this long before touching the VC: a boot that hangs in the bring-up
+ * then still gets the usb shell up first, to watch it with dmesg -w */
+static unsigned int start_delay;
+module_param(start_delay, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(start_delay, "seconds to wait before the VideoCore bring-up (0 = at once)");
+
 static unsigned int debug = 1;
 module_param(debug, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(debug, "log VCHI messages: 1 = bring-up and first frame, 2 = all");
@@ -2114,6 +2120,13 @@ static int vc_thread(void *arg)
 	bool is_cold = false;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (start_delay) {
+		dev_info(vc->dev, "bring-up in %u s (videocore.start_delay)\n", start_delay);
+		schedule_timeout_interruptible(start_delay * HZ);
+		if (kthread_should_stop())
+			return 0;
+		dev_info(vc->dev, "bring-up starts\n");
+	}
 	ret = vc_boot(vc);
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = vchi_connect(vc);
